      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find out how much Steven owes Jeremy, we need to multiply the amount Steven pays per room by the number of rooms Jeremy cleaned. The calculation is as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total amount} = \\text{Amount per room} \\times \\text{Number of rooms}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n- Amount per room = \\(\\frac{11}{2}\\) dollars\n- Number of rooms = \\(\\frac{7}{3}\\)\n\nSo, the calculation is:\n\\[\n\\text{Total amount} = \\frac{11}{2} \\times \\frac{7}{3}\n\\]\n\nTo multiply these fractions, we multiply the numerators together and the denominators together:\n\\[\n\\text{Total amount} = \\frac{11 \\times 7}{2 \\times 3} = \\frac{77}{6}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Steven owes Jeremy \\(\\boxed{\\frac{77}{6}}\\) dollars.",
