      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find out how much Steven owes Jeremy, we need to multiply the amount Steven pays per room by the number of rooms Jeremy cleaned. This can be represented by the following equation:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total amount} = \\text{Amount per room} \\times \\text{Number of rooms cleaned}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n- Amount per room = $\\dfrac{11}{2}$ dollars\n- Number of rooms cleaned = $\\dfrac{7}{3}$\n\nWe can substitute these values into the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total amount} = \\dfrac{11}{2} \\times \\dfrac{7}{3}\n\\]\n\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators together and the denominators together:\n\n\\[\n\\dfrac{11 \\times 7}{2 \\times 3} = \\dfrac{77}{6}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Steven owes Jeremy $\\boxed{\\dfrac{77}{6}}$ dollars.",
